      "Soon, the big bad wolf arrives at the house of sticks. He smells two sweet little pigs inside. He is very happy. \"A double breakfast!\" he thinks.",
      "He knocks on the wooden door: *Knock, knock, knock.*",
      "\"Little pigs, little pigs, let me come in!\" the wolf roars.",
      "Percy and Pinky hold each other. \"No, no!\" they cry. \"Not by the hair on our chinny-chin-chins! We will not let you in!\"",
      "The wolf laughs a dark, terrible laugh. \"Then I will huff, and I will puff, and I will blow your house down!\"",
      "The wolf takes a giant breath. He huffs, and he puffs, and he blows with all his might! *Whoosh!*",
      "The wooden sticks break. The walls fall down. The house of sticks is destroyed.",
      "Percy and Pinky scream loudly. They run as fast as they can through the grass. The wolf runs after them, but the pigs are small and quick. They run straight to Peter's house.",
      "Peter works hard all week. He meets a man carrying a cart of heavy red bricks and wet clay. Peter buys the bricks and clay.",
      "He builds his house slowly and carefully. He lays the red bricks one by one. He makes thick, strong walls. He builds a big stone fireplace and a tall stone chimney. The house has a heavy door made of solid oak wood.",
      "Peter finishes his house on the sixth day. It is a beautiful, strong house of bricks.",
      "Suddenly, Percy and Pinky run to his garden. They are crying and shaking.",
      "\"Peter! Peter!\" they shout. \"The wolf blew our houses down! He ate our straw! He broke our sticks! He is coming to eat us!\"",
      "Peter opens his heavy oak door. \"Do not cry, my brothers. Come inside quickly. My house of bricks is very strong. The wolf cannot hurt us here.\"",
      "The three little pigs run inside and lock the heavy oak door. They bolt the windows.",
      "Soon, the big bad wolf arrives. He looks at the brick house. He smells three little pigs inside. His mouth is watering. \"Three pigs! A giant feast!\"",
