      "In the center of the town, there is a very big, tall tower. It is the Central Clock Tower. The clock on the tower is giant. It has two black hands and twelve golden numbers. The clock makes a loud sound every second: *Tick, tock, tick, tock.*",
      "This giant clock is the heart of the town. Every morning, the chief clockmaker, Mr. Benjamin, winds up the Central Clock. He uses a very special key. The key is made of solid gold. It is the Master Key. If the Central Clock works, all other clocks and toys in the town work, too.",
      "In Clockwork Town lives a young girl named Mia. Mia is nine years old. She has short black hair, brown eyes, and a very curious mind. Mia loves clocks and toys. Her favorite toy is a small clockwork dog named Tick-Tock. Tick-Tock has brown spots and a metal key on his back. Mia winds him up, and Tick-Tock walks around her room. Mia and Tick-Tock are best friends.",
      "One morning, Mia wakes up. She looks at the window. The sun is high in the sky. She looks at her small bedside clock. The clock hands show seven o'clock.",
      "\"Oh!\" Mia says. \"The sun is very bright. It feels like nine o'clock, but my watch says seven.\"",
      "She listens carefully. The house is very quiet. Usually, she hears the giant clock tower from her window: *Tick, tock, tick, tock.* But today, she hears nothing. There is only silence.",
      "Mia winds up her small bedside clock. But the hands do not move. The clock is silent.",
      "She goes to Tick-Tock. She winds up the key on his back. Tick-Tock does not walk. He does not bark. He remains completely still.",
      "Mia is worried. She runs downstairs. Her mother and father are in the kitchen. They are looking out the window.",
      "\"Mother, what is happening?\" Mia asks. \"My clock does not work. Tick-Tock does not move. The tower is silent.\"",
      "Her mother looks sad. \"The Central Clock has stopped, Mia. The whole town has stopped. The street lamps are dark, the bakery oven is cold, and the toy shops are closed.\"",
      "Mia runs out of the house. She goes to the central square. A big crowd of people is standing near the Clock Tower. In front of the tower door, Mr. Benjamin is sitting on a wooden bench. Mr. Benjamin is an old man with white hair and round glasses. He has his head in his hands. He is crying.",
      "Mia walks to him. \"Mr. Benjamin, why did the clock stop? Can you not wind it up?\"",
      "Mr. Benjamin looks up. His eyes are red. \"Oh, Mia,\" he says. \"A terrible thing has happened. The Master Key is gone! Someone stole the golden key last night! Without the Master Key, I cannot wind the Central Clock. And if the clock is silent, the town will sleep forever.\"",
      "\"Where did you lose it?\" Mia asks.",
      "\"I kept it in a velvet box on my table inside the tower,\" Mr. Benjamin says. \"In the morning, the window was open, and the box was empty. I searched the tower, but the key is not here.\"",
      "Mia looks at the high tower. \"Do not cry, Mr. Benjamin,\" she says. \"Tick-Tock and I will find the key. We will bring the music back to Clockwork Town!\"",
      "Mia decides to be a detective. She goes back to her house and gets Tick-Tock. Tick-Tock does not have much power, but Mia carries him in her arms.",
      "\"We need to find clues, Tick-Tock,\" Mia says.",
      "She goes to the back of the Clock Tower. Under the open window of Mr. Benjamin's room, there is a small garden with soft dirt.",
