      "Once upon a time, there is a small, quiet village. The village is surrounded by high green mountains and a beautiful blue river. In this village, the people work very hard. The farmers work in the fields from morning to night. The bakers bake bread all day. The teachers teach the children in the small school.",
      "Sometimes, the people are very tired. Sometimes, they are sad. They work so much that they forget to smile. They forget to look at the beautiful stars at night.",
      "In this village lives a young boy named Oliver. Oliver is ten years old. He has bright blue eyes and hands that are always colorful because he loves to paint. Oliver is a painter.",
      "Oliver lives with his grandmother in a small wooden house at the edge of the forest. Oliver does not have many toys. He does not have a toy train or a clockwork dog. But he has something better. He has a set of magical paints and a special wooden paint brush.",
      "An old, wise traveler gave the brush and the paints to Oliver a long time ago. The traveler said, \"Oliver, your heart is pure. You love to bring happiness to people. These paints are magic. Whatever you paint on a white canvas with this brush will come to life at night to help your friends.\"",
      "Oliver did not believe the traveler at first. But one night, his grandmother was very cold. She had a bad cough. Oliver felt sad. He took his brush and his magic paint. On a large piece of white paper, he painted a beautiful, warm, golden fireplace with bright orange flames.",
      "He went to sleep. During the night, a wonderful thing happened. The painting disappeared from the paper. In the morning, the wooden house was warm and cozy, and his grandmother's cough was gone! She smiled and hugged Oliver.",
      "\"Your room is so warm, Oliver,\" she said.",
      "Oliver knew then that the traveler's words were true. He was the Boy Who Painted Dreams.",
      "From that day on, Oliver looked for ways to help his neighbors. He walked through the village every afternoon. He looked at the people's faces. He listened to their stories.",
      "If someone was sad or had a problem, Oliver went home to his small room. He took his magic brush and painted a dream to solve their problem.",
      "One day, Mr. Thomas, the old farmer, was very sad. He stood in his dry brown field. \"Oh,\" he said to Oliver. \"The sun is too hot. There is no rain. My corn is dry and yellow. If it does not rain soon, I will have no food to sell at the market.\"",
      "Oliver went home. He sat at his table. He took his brush and his blue paint. On the paper, he painted soft, grey clouds and gentle, cool raindrops falling on green corn plants.",
      "That night, while the village slept, a gentle rain fell only on Mr. Thomas's field. The next morning, the corn was green and strong. Mr. Thomas was very happy. He danced in his field. \"A miracle!\" he shouted.",
      "Another day, a little girl named Lily was crying in the street. \"Oliver, I lost my little white cat, Snowflake,\" she said, crying. \"I looked everywhere, but I cannot find her.\"",
