      "\"Oh no!\" Oliver cries. \"How can I paint the sun without yellow paint? I have blue, red, and green, but I need yellow for the sun!\"",
      "Oliver looks at his cat. \"Brush, we must find something yellow to make yellow paint. What is yellow in the village?\"",
      "Oliver searches the house. He finds a lemon in the kitchen. He squeezes the lemon, but the juice is clear, not yellow enough for magic paint.",
      "He goes to the village streets in the cold fog. He looks for yellow things. But the yellow flowers are closed and grey in the cold.",
      "Suddenly, Oliver remembers something. \"The Golden Valley!\" he says. \"Deep in the forest, there is a valley. It has special golden flowers that shine even in the dark! I can use those flowers to make magic yellow paint!\"",
      "Oliver puts on his warm red coat. He takes a small empty glass jar and walks into the dark, foggy forest. His black cat, Brush, walks next to him.",
      "The forest is silent and spooky in the thick grey fog. The trees look like giant dark ghosts. Oliver is a little afraid, but he thinks of the cold, sad people in his village. He walks brave and strong.",
